    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0538" n="366" xml:id="pg366"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7757</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Panama</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Price</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-13T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 13, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 7, 10 p.m.,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d536-f1"/> and November 7, 8
                        p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d536-f2"/> In view of these two telegrams a formal
                    declaration of war is regarded as practically unnecessary. For your information
                    it is not deemed desirable that Panama make a formal declaration of war.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
